WEBVTT

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.240
How's this?

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.150
Is it <i>still</i> crooked?!

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.630
Don't have to be so fussy...

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.190
There, how's that?

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:16.660
Meowww!

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.210
Due to Participation in Regional Tournament Today
 Closed for the Day
 Please come again  by Manager

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.700
Yesss! I got a Royal Paladin!

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.450
What are you doing, Brother?

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.750
I opened a new booster pack. Look!

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.190
Wha...?! You're just doing that <i>now</i>?!

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.560
Uh...Yeah.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.350
No matter how new it is, if you just 
randomly put a card in your deck,

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.050
it won't make you any stronger!

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:45.130
You gotta test-play it first, and 
make sure that your deck balances out.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.940
Yeah, I understand that, but...

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.940
No, you don't get it at all!

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:50.940
Today is the regional tournament!

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.650
No, I know that too, but...

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.840
Today's fight is a three-person 
team competition.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.570
Kai, Kamui and Misaki are playing.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.460
I'm just an alternate.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.330
Well, we'd better get going.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:08.870
Huh?

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.190
Where's Misaki?

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:14.970
Oh, she'll meet up with us later.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.300
Oh...

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.510
And here we go.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:21.590
Yeahhh!

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:22.970
Man, you're slow!

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.580
Hmm...

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.680
You think I should take this one out?

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.720
You put in a grade 3,

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.530
so if you don't take out a grade 3 in its 
place, the balance will be out of whack.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.000
I see. Then how about this one?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:19.670
Mmm, you've got a lot of cards that go well 
with that one, so I think you should leave it in.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.560
Um...Then...

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.270
Quadri...foglio?

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:23.890
Huh?

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:28.270
Yep. It's the Italian word 
for "four-leaf clover".

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.520
Kai, Kamui, Aichi and Misaki.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.170
The four of you will combine 
your strength to fight.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:37.290
Team Quadrifoglio.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.480
Great naming sense, isn't it?

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.590
Team Quadrifoglio...?

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.430
"Team Card Capital" would've worked, too...

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.740
But that doesn't really 
have any zing, you know?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.250
Quadri...Qua...Qu...Quad...

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.300
It's too hard to say!

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.380
I guess you're right.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:58.970
Then what do you say we 
shorten it to "Team Q4"?

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.420
Q4?

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.220
Hey, that's kinda cool!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.090
Yeah, it sounds good to me.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.950
What do you think, Kai?

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.810
The name doesn't really matter.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.640
Then it's settled.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.270
Whoa! Manager!

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.510
You're driving too fast!

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:21.030
Team Q4 Heads for the Regional Tournament!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.750
There it is, just up ahead.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:25.450
Oh!

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:41.190
Brother Aichi, this is your first time 
attending <i>and</i> playing in a regional tournament, right?

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:45.250
Y-Yeah. I didn't imagine it'd be 
held in a huge center like this...

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:48.610
Awesome!

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:49.700
Let's go!

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:50.570
Okay!

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.920
What's this...?

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.100
A Motion Figure System.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.520
It's a device that makes a 3D representation 
of fights and units working together.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:01.230
Is it your first time seeing this, too?

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:05.310
I've seen a machine that's 
sort of similar to this.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.710
You're talking about that 
shop you went to once, right?

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.590
"PSY", I think it's called?

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:11.340
Yes.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:14.850
Whoa! There's a shop that has one of these?!

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:17.550
You oughta have one at Card Capital!

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.800
I couldn't afford it!

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.510
Hello, everyone!

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.370
Wha...?!

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.250
Nice to meet you! I'm Kourin!

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.730
My name is Suiko.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.020
I'm Rekka!

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.480
The three of us together...

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.730
...are Ultra-rare!

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.440
U-Ultra-rare...?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:45.750
Welcome to today's third Kanto region 
Vanguard Championship Tournament!

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:49.170
If you win here, you'll go on 
to the national championship!

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:52.130
I think you've got tough 
matches waiting for you...

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.970
But everyone, do your best!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.370
What are <i>they</i> doing here?

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.590
They're like an idol group. 
They made their debut recently.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:03.120
It's seems they're promoting this tournament.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.300
Why, do you know them?

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.440
Yes, a little.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:09.680
But that smiling face...

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.100
It's like she's a different person entirely.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.600
Kourin!

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.730
Cut it out, that's pathetic!

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.350
Shut up! Don't get in the way 
of my fated reunion with her!

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:22.440
The thing is, that's only an image of her!

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.280
I've known ever since we first met.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:28.200
That girl has the power to draw people in.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.080
You see?! My judgment wasn't off!

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.430
I just know Ultra-rare's gonna be big!

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.970
Especially Kourin!

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:36.980
Well, see you at Nationals!

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.980
We'll be waiting!

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.510
Okay, I'll be there!

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.210
Morikawa!

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.490
Huh?

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:47.330
You finally got here, Aichi?!

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:49.710
Yep! And I see Izaki's here, too!

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:52.700
Sure! A classmate of mine's 
playing in the tournament.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.190
I had to come to cheer you on!

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:56.800
We're here, too!

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:58.470
Don't forget about us!

00:06:58.470 --> 00:06:59.940
DF, yo!

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.310
You guys!

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.910
Yeah, the gang's all here!

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:06.440
Kamuiii!!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.780
Oof!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.150
Kamui! Kamui! I love you!

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:13.280
Who the hell is she?!

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:16.110
I'm not "she", I'm Nagisa!

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:19.190
I'm Kamui's... girlfriend!

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:19.800
Ack!

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.900
G-Girlfriend?!

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:24.760
Pretty mature for an elementary 
school student, huh?

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.670
Pull yourself together, Morikawa.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:27.430
Heh!

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:29.620
No need to worry about me!

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:33.140
What, you think something like 
that would send me into shock?

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:33.980
Uh...

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:38.040
After all, I've got Kourin!

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.010
You're living in dreamland!

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.350
Long time no see, Sendou!

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:46.240
You actually showed up, 
instead of running away!

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.900
I respect you for that, anyway! Ka-boom!

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.650
Team Handsome!

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.430
Big brother!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:56.510
Great Kamui, are you okay?!

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:57.790
OK, yo?!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:02.000
So this is the team that 
Kamui chose over us...

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.130
Hmph. Looks like a bunch of feebs!

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.720
Definitely not in our league!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.070
Hahaha!

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.520
The weaker the dog, the more it howls.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.140
What was that?!

00:08:14.470 --> 00:08:17.900
Whoa! Hold on! We can't fight in here!

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.470
Or at least not that kind of fight...

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:26.480
Listen, I don't know who they're 
gonna put us up against,

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:29.290
but you guys better not lose 
until we face each other.

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.570
I would say the same for you.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.500
Gotta get the last word in, huh?

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.160
I like you, kid.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.100
Let's go!

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:41.190
See you later, Kamui!

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:48.050
Okay, the teams that the computer's randomly 
chosen to pit against each other are...

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.660
But before that...

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:55.240
I should've introduced myself before.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:59.520
I'm your host, MC Miya!

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:03.190
Nobody cares, just hurry up 
and announce the pairings!

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:04.800
All right, back to the computer...

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:08.230
The two teams facing each other in the first 
fight of the 3rd Kanto Region Tournament are...

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:09.480
Over here!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.490
The first two teams are...

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.690
Team Q4
 Three Blacks

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.560
Three Blacks?

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:22.110
So we're squaring off against you first, huh?

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:22.670
Huh?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.050
Wh-Who the heck are you guys?

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.460
Ask and ye shall be answered!

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.300
I'm Kurosawa!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.280
I'm Kurosaki!

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:36.880
I'm Kuroda!

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.090
The three of us together...

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:43.860
You all have "kuro", or "black", in 
your names, so "Three Blacks", huh?

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.090
I get it!

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:48.110
And on top of that, they're 
wearing black cloaks!

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:48.810
Huh?

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.320
W-We wanted to explain all that.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.360
Uh, sorry!

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.000
Well, it's kind of a name 
that begs for commentary!

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.350
But aside from that, what's the getup for?!

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.410
I'm glad you asked! This is...

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:03.540
You're black magicians?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.420
Ah!

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.060
What did I say?!

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:07.290
I'm sorry!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:11.340
Black magicians, my foot! 
They're just cosplayers!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.890
C-Cosplayers?!

00:10:12.890 --> 00:10:17.070
Don't hurt our pride by applying 
that vulgar word to us!

00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.480
Vulgar...?!

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.880
Better not let a cosplayer 
catch you saying that!

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.740
Good point! It's like you 
and your love for ninjas!

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:27.180
Well, it's not like that's <i>cosplay</i>...

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:30.600
Although if I were gonna do 
cosplay, it'd be as a ninja...

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.620
This is an insult!

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:33.990
No, that's fine.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:36.730
Let him talk while he still can.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.780
'Cause once the fight starts, 
he'll be trembling with terror!

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:44.790
Don't tell me you guys can 
actually use black magic?!

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.160
Yeah, right!

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.440
How old are you?!

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:48.920
Dream when you're sleeping!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:54.260
We're saying we're gonna pin you 
down with our skill at Vanguard!

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:57.990
See you at the fight, Team Q4.

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:01.090
You guys are gonna lose!

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.800
Hey, Morikawa!

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.650
So they're our team's first opponents...

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:09.250
Huh? Come to think of it, 
Misaki isn't here yet.

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:12.970
Yeah. She told me she wouldn't be 
able to get here 'til the afternoon.

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:16.310
I think she'll be able to make 
it in time for the final fight.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.510
Oh, really?

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:22.870
Wait, what?! Then what about the tournament?!

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:25.200
The first round is gonna start soon!

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:26.940
No problem!

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:29.200
We've got three on our team, right?

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.110
Three...?

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:32.180
Um...

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:34.790
Huh?

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.240
W-Whaaat?!

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:03.120
Brother, no need to be that nervous!

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.430
Y-Yeah...

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.320
That's right!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.710
Even if <i>you</i> lose...

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:11.930
As long as the other two 
win, your team will advance!

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:13.040
Mm-hm!

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.830
You're not encouraging him!

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:19.300
Hey! Don't talk about losing 
before we even start, Lose-umi!

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.550
The name is Katsumi, you little...!

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:22.900
Aichi!

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:23.550
Oh!

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.160
Manager...

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:26.840
Use these.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.710
Gloves?

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:30.890
They're Vanguard fighting gloves.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:35.390
Put it on when you fight using 
the Motion Figure System.

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:40.120
The story goes that the crystal on 
the glove is from the planet Cray.

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:44.040
When that crystal works with the System...

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:48.060
...you'll be invited to a world you've only 
known in your imagination up 'til now.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.660
That's how the person in charge 
of the machine described it to me.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.490
Thank you!

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.730
I feel a little better now.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.210
Manager! Do you have 
orange?! I'll take orange!

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.610
I sure do.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:00.880
Oh, awesome!

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.710
The red one is for Kai...and 
the green for Misaki.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:06.230
The first fight is about to begin.

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:08.930
The first fighter of each team, 
please proceed to the console.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.950
Good luck, Brother!

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:21.610
Console?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.290
So you're the first fighter, huh?

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:38.260
Um...

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:40.040
You're Kuro...

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.470
What was it again?

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.850
It's Kurosawa!

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:45.670
I just told you a couple of minutes 
ago, so you forgetting is totally rude!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.420
S-Sorry!

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:48.600
But...

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.550
I couldn't tell you apart...

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:54.220
All right, fighters, let's shuffle!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.550
Let's Vanguard!

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:58.460
First fight, begin!

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.680
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:09.010
Whoaaa!

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:11.080
It <i>is</i> more exciting with that machine!

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:14.910
Nice... If only Card Capital 
had something like this…

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.120
This is...

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:25.270
What's wrong? You get to go first.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.780
No sense dawdling.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.300
A Kagero deck...

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.610
I draw! And ride Wingal!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.250
I move Barcgal!

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.670
With Barcgal's skill, I call Flogal!

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.270
I draw!

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:46.580
I ride the Embodiment of Armor, Bahr!

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.480
This pattern...

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.360
Brother...

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.410
What is he afraid of?

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.450
Is it the same as Kai's?

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:04.290
What should I do? It was a mistake 
to enter this tournament!

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:09.430
I don't know what you're scared 
of, but I'm not gonna hold back!

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.790
I call the Demonic Dragon Madonna, Joka!

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.370
Joka?!

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.420
What? Do you have 
something aqainst Joka?

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.680
N-No...

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.260
Brother, get a hold of yourself!

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:23.390
This is no time to get cold feet!

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:26.230
But you gotta admit, it is a little scary!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.700
What, you're afraid of snakes?

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:32.270
What's wrong with Aichi?

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.220
This is the first time I've seen that unit.

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:39.040
The same deck as Kai, but 
new units on top of that...

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:42.640
He's shaken up by trifling nonsense...

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:45.530
Then let's go!

00:15:45.530 --> 00:15:47.470
My target is Wingal!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.090
Drive trigger check!

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.070
D-Damage trigger check!

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.460
I attack with Joka!

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:00.240
I guard with Epona!

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.270
My turn's over.

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:09.560
What should I do?

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:12.490
How is he going to fight me after this turn?

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:20.340
It's no good! I have no idea!

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:22.790
I'll do my usual...

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.040
Stand up, my avatar!

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:28.170
I ride Blaster Blade!

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:35.840
I call Wingal!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:41.150
Wingal powers up Blaster Blade 
with its boost and skill!

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.230
Drive trigger check!

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:49.020
No trigger...

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.000
Damage trigger check!

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:55.780
No trigger here either.

00:16:56.610 --> 00:17:00.160
I attack your Bahr with my 
Barcgal, boosted by Flogal!

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.120
Damage trigger...

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:08.660
2 damage, huh?

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.570
Now you're on track.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.040
But here's where I throw you off for good.

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:16.100
Now you'll feel my power!

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:19.840
I ride the Dragon Knight, Nehalem!

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.500
Then I call Tejas and Jarran!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:29.410
Joka moves back.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:30.730
He moved it...

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:34.030
In the open space, I call Berserk Dragon!

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:40.860
Berserk Dragon's Counterblast!

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:44.540
I see. This guy isn't just all talk.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.540
Huh?!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:49.750
I would like for the Wingal 
at the back to withdraw!

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:51.160
Wha...?!

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:51.740
Ah!

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.770
On top of that, I activate Joka's skill!

00:17:57.770 --> 00:18:01.600
As long as your rear guard is 
defeated by the skill of my unit...

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.460
Joka's power is +3000!

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:10.460
The Counterblast from calling 
the Berserk Dragon...

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.760
It's even powered up Joka.

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:14.740
With just a grade 2 card...!

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.000
That's a remarkable combo!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.870
Do you think this is as bad as it gets?

00:18:22.110 --> 00:18:25.670
You know the skill I activated 
to drop your rear guard?

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.270
Joka isn't my only unit that has it!

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:27.870
Huh?!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.470
I activate a skill!

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:32.120
Gaze at the magnificent dance of death!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.570
Superior Ride!

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:36.250
The Demonic Dragon Berserker, Yaksha!

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:49.240
Even though he didn't reach grade 2 first, 
he got to grade 3 before Brother Aichi!

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:51.040
The combo was <i>this</i> long?!

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.550
That's beyond scary!

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.140
Maybe he really is using black magic!

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:58.020
I don't think so!

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:00.370
And now I'll change the focus of my attack!

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:05.280
First, I attack your Barcgal with my 
Berserker Dragon, boosted by Joka!

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:11.710
Then I attack Flogal with 
Tejas, boosted by Jarran!

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.460
Huh?!

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.810
Flogal is in the rear-guard!

00:19:16.850 --> 00:19:18.630
Why is he allowed to attack?!

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:21.920
That's Tejas's skill!

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.690
That's a troublesome unit!

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:28.400
What's more, Jarran's skill adds 
+4000 to the power of Tejas!

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:33.370
All that's left is you!

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.430
Twin drive check!

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:40.100
Yes!

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:41.450
No trigger!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:45.530
It seems that your luck 
hasn't given out yet...

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:50.690
Damage trigger check!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:09.040
Enter the fray, king of all knights!

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:13.770
The King of Knights, Alfred!

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:18.750
All right, it's Alfred!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:21.030
And now Aichi's at grade 3, too!

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.950
This is no time to celebrate.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:23.320
Mm?

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:27.790
Alfred has finally appeared, but 
he doesn't have a single ally around him.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:28.720
Ah...

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:35.170
I see! For each Royal Paladin in the 
rear-guard, Alfred's power would be raised 2000!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:39.670
At this rate, all he can do is attack with 
Alfred at his normal power level of 10000!

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:42.920
As expected, you came with Alfred, huh?

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.000
Oh, no...

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:48.560
Oh, yeah. You're using Royal Paladins, so 
figuring out your strategy was a cinch.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:52.170
That's why I cleared the 
field of all your allies!

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:00.150
So now what are you gonna do?

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.310
I have allies!

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:07.040
I call the Solitary Knight, Gancelot!

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:08.880
The Little Sage, Marron!

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:10.910
The Yggdrasil Maiden, Elaine!

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:14.210
And the Knight of Truth, Gordon!

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.840
Thattaboy, Aichi!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:23.000
He still had good cards left!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.380
Well, the situation is not as optimistic as it seems.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:26.880
Eh?

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:29.880
Look at Aichi's hand.

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:31.720
His hand...

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:32.800
He's got nothing!

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:33.480
Mm.

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:37.880
He was driven to the point where 
he had to use up all his cards.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:41.640
And even with that, Alfred's 
power is only 18000.

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:44.290
Definitely not full power...

00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:47.590
He's a tough fighter.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:51.110
But I guess that's to be expected 
at the regional tournament...

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.920
On top of that, he just put Gordon
 into the deck this morning...

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:57.080
What's that mean?

00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:02.540
The deck that Brother's using now 
has never even been test-played before!

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:04.620
It's a deck he just put together!

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:07.060
W-What?!

00:22:07.060 --> 00:22:10.150
Nobody knows whether that deck...

00:22:10.150 --> 00:22:11.940
...works well or not!

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:52.760
Vanguard fight glove...

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:56.830
How do I look? I feel like 
I'm an F1 driver! Cool!

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:57.410
Yeah!

00:23:57.410 --> 00:24:01.920
But I just wanted to cheer you guys on with 
your fights. Instead, I'm the first fighter!

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:03.040
Don't worry!

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.880
I'm the general and that 
jerk Kai is a soldier.

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:07.200
So you just have fun out there!

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:10.260
Th-Thanks, but this guy is strong!

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:12.440
Next time: New Allies!

00:24:12.440 --> 00:24:15.550
Alfred... I have an image of you and 
me achieving victory with our allies!

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:18.440
Brother, shift gears! Put 
the pedal to the metal!
